+-      "body": "Request changes on PR #124 (design(0003)). Re-run the design pass with the decision and the corrections below; keep intent.md unchanged.\n\n**Decision on the open flagged concern**\n1. Concern 1 (the `class` tag's vocabulary): decided. The class is free text in kebab-case; `index.py build` normalises it (lower-case; spaces and underscores to hyphens; one heading per normalised value), so a spelling drift cannot create a second heading. For an incident the weekly scan filed, the class is the `class` field of `evidence/scan-finding.json`. No controlled vocabulary now: no lesson exists to name one from (decision 17), and a list would be a guardrail edit on every project. Revisit when a project has ten lessons. Rewrite the item so it starts with \"decided\".\n\n**spec.md**\n2. Gate scope: the new lesson, eval and `check` sub-checks run at gate (e) only. State the guard explicitly: `ctx.status.entry_route == \"incident\" and ctx.phase == \"e\"`. Today the incident branch of `check_artifacts` sits inside the `intent.md` block, which every gate (a) to (f) runs, so without the guard every incident parks at (f) with \"lesson missing\" and `tests/test_gate.py::test_gate_f_waits_for_the_owner_s_triage_with_the_finding_and_its_route` turns red. Name that test as the regression guard.\n3. One \"what I need from you\" line per failure: `check_artifacts` joins every problem into one failure with one fixed need text, so the requirement cannot be met inside that function as the Design says. Decided: a separate check `lesson_and_eval` registered at phase \"e\" in `CHECKS_BY_PHASE`, returning one CheckResult whose `need` lists one line per problem. Drop the \"no new CHECKS_BY_PHASE entry\" constraint. Add a test that asserts the rendered what-I-need text.\n4. `(stale)` and a byte-exact `check` contradict each other: the day a lesson passes `stale_after`, `build` output changes with no file changed, `check` fails, and the maintain run falls back to every file until the