-      "body": "Request changes on PR #124 (design(0003)). Re-run the design pass with the decision and the corrections below; keep intent.md unchanged.\n\n**Decision on the open flagged concern**\n1. Concern 1 (the `class` tag's vocabulary): decided. The class is free text in kebab-case; `index.py build` normalises it (lower-case; spaces and underscores to hyphens; one heading per normalised value), so a spelling drift cannot create a second heading. For an incident the weekly scan filed, the class is the `class` field of `evidence/scan-finding.json`. No controlled vocabulary now: no lesson exists to name one from (decision 17), and a list would be a guardrail edit on every project. Revisit when a project has ten lessons. Rewrite the item so it starts with \"decided\".\n\n**spec.md**\n2. Gate scope: the new lesson, eval and `check` sub-checks run at gate (e) only. State the guard explicitly: `ctx.status.entry_route == \"incident\" and ctx.phase == \"e\"`. Today the incident branch of `check_artifacts` sits inside the `intent.md` block, which every gate (a) to (f) runs, so without the guard every incident parks at (f) with \"lesson missing\" and `tests/test_gate.py::test_gate_f_waits_for_the_owner_s_triage_with_the_finding_and_its_route` turns red. Name that test as the regression guard.\n3. One \"what I need from you\" line per failure: `check_artifacts` joins every problem into one failure with one fixed need text, so the requirement cannot be met inside that function as the Design says. Decided: a separate check `lesson_and_eval` registered at phase \"e\" in `CHECKS_BY_PHASE`, returning one CheckResult whose `need` lists one line per problem. Drop the \"no new CHECKS_BY_PHASE entry\" constraint. Add a test that asserts the rendered what-I-need text.\n4. `(stale)` and a byte-exact `check` contradict each other: the day a lesson passes `stale_after`, `build` output changes with no file changed, `check` fails, and the maintain run falls back to every file until the next incident. Decided: `check` compares the index with the `(stale)` suffixes stripped from both sides, and `build`/`check` take `--today YYYY-MM-DD` for the tests. Write it under Requirements and Acceptance.\n5. The glob \"every `lessons/*.md`\" includes `README.md` (copied into every project by `/sdlc-init`) and `index.md` itself. Exclude both by name. State that an `## Unsorted` entry (a file without a parsable frontmatter) does not fail `check`; it is listed and `check` prints a one-line note per Unsorted file. A frontmatter that does not parse is Unsorted with the parser's error in the note, never a crash.\n6. Frontmatter notation: the project's YAML reader (`plugin/state/yamlish.py`) refuses flow style (`fixed: {pr: 42}` raises \"flow mappings are not supported\") and truncates an unquoted value at ` #`. Require block style for every nested field, and double quotes on `title` and `description`, in the README example and in step 0b. Read lesson files with `utf-8-sig` before the frontmatter split.\n7. Concern 3 (Windows newline stability) was closed on a wrong basis: `yamlish.dump_file` dumps YAML and cannot write the markdown index, and a concern may be closed only by a policy or the owner, not by code. Reopen it and close it as decided by the owner with the real mechanism, stated as a requirement: the index is written with `write_text(..., newline=\"\\n\")`, `check` compares text read in universal-newline mode (a CRLF checkout must not false-positive), and every link uses `as_posix()` (the intent's forward-slash constraint, which the spec dropped).\n8. `runbook` source: the \"resolved route\" reasoning does not hold (`Resolved.route` is always the proposal's route; `runbook_authorized_by` is set only for `go` routes). The source is `evidence/proposal.json: route` when `evidence/runbook-<name>.json` exists with `status: ran`; absent otherwise (failed or go-requested included). Make Requirements and Design say the same thing.\n9. Scan-filed incidents: an incident the weekly scan files carries `evidence/scan-finding.json`, not `detection.json`; `finding.read_any` maps it to metric `security: <class>`, rule `scan`, tier 3, and there are no failed-run URLs. Add one requirement: `detected` is read through `finding.read_any`, the `detection` source points at whichever file exists, `run-<n>` sources are absent for a scan incident, and the class tag is the scan's `class` field (item 1).\n10. Determinism the build would otherwise guess, write each down: the index line is `* [title](file) - description. Tier n, Mon yyyy.` (the proposal's); \"newest first\" sorts by `detected.at` descending, then file name; `## Unsorted` comes after `## Retired`; `build` with zero lessons writes the heading and one line \"No lessons yet.\"; the gate finds the lesson by `lessons/*-<slug>.md` (the month varies); the required fields are every field of the table except `runbook` and `supersedes`, which are optional; \"the eval case exists\" means `evals/cases/<id>-<slug>/prompt.md` and `checks.yaml` both exist. Acceptance says \"three sub-checks\" and lists five: make the count match.\n11. Restore these intent sentences the spec dropped, one Requirements bullet each: a stale lesson is still read and the maintain run says when it relied on one; `description` is one sentence in the metric's terms; a hand edit of the index is undone by the next `build`; `/sdlc-init` copies the README as today; no workflow template changes; the sample stays frozen; decision 17 unchanged.\n12. Add the `supersedes` rule to the deploy requirement: when the new lesson carries `supersedes: <file>`, step 0b sets the earlier lesson's `status: retired` and adds `retired_by: <the new file>` in the same commit; the gate (e) sub-check verifies the superseded file exists and reads `retired`.\n13. Both command files' `allowed-tools` frontmatter gains `Bash(python \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/plugin/lessons/index.py\" *)`, and the body quotes the call the same way (the instruction test requires it). CI is unaffected; a by-hand run would otherwise prompt.\n14. Citations to correct: `HANDOFF.md:60-61` is item 11 (item 4 is the row at line 42); `tests/test_evals.py:701-767` are the `case.py new` CLI tests, not instruction tests; `tests/test_gate.py:2346-2364` is gate (f) coverage, not (e), and no (e) incident fixture exists yet (say to build one with `_ctx(tmp_path, phase=\"e\")` and `entry_route=\"incident\"`); `docs/notes/1.md`'s frontmatter is flat (`generated.at` is one key).\n\n**plan.md**\n15. Add `plugin/lessons/__init__.py` to \"## Files that change\" (every plugin subpackage has one; the plan-sync exemption covers `*.md` only, so step 1's commit is denied without it).\n16. The \"No change to \u2026\" paragraph wraps so that one line starts with `17), to \\`plugin/detect/**\\``, and the gate's file-list parser reads it as a numbered item: `plugin/detect/**` is currently counted as a planned file (the opposite of the sentence, and the port-list path HANDOFF tracks). Move that paragraph to Risks and make sure no continuation line in \"## Files that change\" starts with a digit, `-` or `*`.\n17. Reflect items 2 to 13 in the file items: the phase guard and the separate check in the `checks.py` item and Risk 2; `build` excluding README and index, `--today`, the Unsorted rule, newline and `as_posix()` in the `index.py` item; the `supersedes` rule, the scan shape, block style and the `allowed-tools` line in the `sdlc-deploy.md` item; the `allowed-tools` line in the `sdlc-maintain.md` item.\n18. Tests: `tests/test_lessons.py` adds README.md present and ignored, index.md ignored, malformed frontmatter to Unsorted without a crash, a CRLF index on disk passing `check`, zero lessons, the stale marker with `--today`, class normalisation; `tests/test_gate.py` adds the (e) incident fixture, the pass case, one test per failure, the rendered what-I-need text, and the (f) regression; if `artifacts.py` needs the eval case names, import them from `plugin/evals/case.py` instead of duplicating.\n19. Risks: add the clock dependence of `(stale)` (item 4); fix Risk 6's fact (this repository has no root `lessons/`; only `template/lessons/README.md` exists; the conclusion stands); reword Risk 3's mitigation as instruction-text assertions in `tests/test_commands_and_skills.py` (pytest cannot assert the model's Evidence line); state that the build starts only after concern 1 is closed and that the free-text answer leaves the file list unchanged.\n20. Order of work step 2 says \"three new incident sub-checks\"; align the count with the file item.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
